cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or data, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Exam Timed-Release Benchmark: a pre-registered matched benchmark of threshold key release through a smart contract, a replicated coordinator and a central key server"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-25
authors:
  - family-names: Aboessa
    given-names: Ahmed A.
    affiliation: "Department of Mathematics and Computer Science, Faculty of Science, Menoufia University, Egypt"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ahmedcs123/exam-timed-release-benchmark"
abstract: >-
  Code, pre-registration, raw run records and analysis scripts for a pre-registered benchmark of timed release of
  examination-paper keys with Shamir threshold sharing, comparing a Solidity contract on a four-validator Hyperledger
  Besu QBFT network, a REST coordinator over a three-node etcd cluster, and a central key server. Includes 280 measured
  runs, nine scripted fault and security tests, an exploratory network-delay cell and static analysis of the contract.
  All data are synthetic. Data, results and documentation are licensed under CC BY 4.0 (see LICENSE-DATA.md).
keywords:
  - examination paper leakage
  - timed release
  - threshold secret sharing
  - smart contracts
  - Hyperledger Besu
  - etcd
  - benchmark
  - pre-registration
